# Asher Project State

Asher is a mod manager for Dust: An Elysian Tail. The frontend is an **Electron** app (`Asher.Electron`). The backend is a C# console process (`Asher.Host`) communicating over **JSONL on stdin/stdout**.

## Completed (do not reimplement)

- Electron shell: sidebar, home hub, settings, patch manager, game setup
- Install / uninstall / launch flows through JSONL contract
- Localization (en-US, pt-BR, es) in renderer `localization.js`
- Theme (Light / Dark) in renderer `theme.js`
- Material Symbols Outlined icons (self-hosted font, `icons.js`)
- Settings auto-save, preference-only reset, browse path
- Install Finish UX with optional launch + minimize
- `BackupEnabled` gates `CreateBackup` in `GameInstallationService`
- `setModEnabled` validates mod existence in `PatchManagerService`
- Incremental mod-list rendering (no full DOM rebuild on toggle)
- Toast notifications (`action-banner.js`, top-right stack)
- `markInstalled` / `markUninstalled` contract methods (replaced fragile settings merge)
- Install payload bundled via MSBuild (`install-payload/` beside `Asher.Host.exe`)
- Zip + unpacked Distribution packaging (`npm run dist` → `Distribution/`; GitHub publish via `npm run publish` + `private/GH_TOKEN`)
- Packaged manager self-deploy to `game/Asher/Asher.App/` on Finish, then relaunch from that copy
- GitHub Releases update check / zip apply for the installed manager (Settings → Check for updates)
- Uninstall preserves `Asher/Asher.App` (and logs/backup) so the in-game manager is never self-deleted while running; user can reinstall from the same app

## Retired (do not recreate)

- WPF UI: `Asher.App`, `Asher.UserInterface`, `Asher.Localization` — deleted
- WPF-only services: `ManagerLaunch`, `Shortcut`, `InstallationState`, `NavigationItemsManager` (manager deploy/relaunch restored in Electron main, not those C# services)
- `PrepareDistribution.ps1` — WPF-era packaging script
- Prism / MaterialDesign / WPF dependencies in `Asher.Core`
- Portable-as-primary packaging (replaced by zip / Distribution folder)

## Deferred

- Full install wizard stepper chrome
- Content patcher UI (no backend exists)
- Desktop shortcut creation after install

